---
import MarketingLayout from "../layouts/MarketingLayout.astro";
---

<MarketingLayout
  title="Website privacy"
  description="How this public documentation website differs from a sitter’s Boopity installation."
>
  <article class="wrap max-w-3xl py-16">
    <h1 class="display text-5xl">Website privacy</h1>
    <p class="mt-8 leading-relaxed">
      This marketing and documentation site has no account registration,
      advertising trackers, analytics scripts, or payment forms. Documentation
      search runs in your browser. The guide theme selector may remember your
      preference in browser storage.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-5 leading-relaxed">
      Links to GitHub, the demo, and other websites take you to separate
      services with their own data handling. Hosting providers may process
      ordinary request information, such as your IP address, to serve a website.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-10 text-2xl font-semibold">
      Your sitter’s website is separate
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 leading-relaxed">
      Each Boopity installation is operated independently. For questions about
      client records, bookings, or payments, contact the business operating that
      installation. Do not enter real client information into a demonstration
      installation.
    </p>
  </article>
</MarketingLayout>
